{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hecke_eigenvalues_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hecke_eigenvalues_forced","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuaternionFromHecke.lean#L104-L118","doc":"The Hecke relation σ² = (q - q⁻¹)σ + 1 implies the\neigenvalue equation lam² = (q - q⁻¹)lam + 1, which factors as\n(lam - q)(lam + q⁻¹) = 0. This FORCES the eigenvalues to be\nexactly {+q, -q⁻¹} — there is no freedom to choose them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke.classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke.classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuaternionFromHecke.lean#L100-L100","doc":"At q = 1, the antisymmetric eigenvalue is -1, recovering\nthe quaternion relation i² = -1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke.hecke_eigenvalue_antisym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke.hecke_eigenvalue_antisym","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuaternionFromHecke.lean#L97-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke.hecke_eigenvalue_sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke.hecke_eigenvalue_sym","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuaternionFromHecke.lean#L96-L96","doc":"The Hecke generator σ acts on V ⊗ V with eigenvalues\n+q (on S²V) and -q⁻¹ (on Λ²V). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke.antisymmetric_subspace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke.antisymmetric_subspace","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuaternionFromHecke.lean#L93-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke.symmetric_subspace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke.symmetric_subspace","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuaternionFromHecke.lean#L92-L92","doc":"V ⊗ V decomposes as S²V ⊕ Λ²V (Clebsch-Gordan). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke.V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke.V","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuaternionFromHecke.lean#L90-L90","doc":"The fundamental representation V = R² (spin-½). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke.q_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke.q_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuaternionFromHecke.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke.q","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuaternionFromHecke.lean#L87-L87","doc":"The substrate parameter q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke.mk","kind":"ctor","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuaternionFromHecke.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QuaternionFromHecke","kind":"class","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuaternionFromHecke.lean#L73-L102","doc":"The quaternionic structure on V ⊗ V induced by the Hecke\ngenerator. This is the categorical statement that ℍ emerges\nfrom the R-matrix decomposition, not from an ad hoc choice.\n\nThe key content: the Hecke relation σ² = (q - q⁻¹)σ + 1\nforces the eigenspace decomposition V ⊗ V = V_q ⊕ V_{-q⁻¹},\nand the eigenvalue -q⁻¹ on the antisymmetric component\nrecovers i² = j² = k² = -1 at q = 1.\n\nAt q ≠ 1: the q-deformed quaternion algebra ℍ_q has the\nmodified relation i² = j² = k² = -q⁻¹ (NOT -1), which is\nthe Hecke-deformation of the classical quaternion algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeEigenvalues.antisymmetric_eigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeEigenvalues.antisymmetric_eigenvalue","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuaternionFromHecke.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeEigenvalues.symmetric_eigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeEigenvalues.symmetric_eigenvalue","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuaternionFromHecke.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeEigenvalues.q_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeEigenvalues.q_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuaternionFromHecke.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeEigenvalues.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeEigenvalues.q","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuaternionFromHecke.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeEigenvalues.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeEigenvalues.mk","kind":"ctor","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuaternionFromHecke.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeEigenvalues","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeEigenvalues","kind":"structure","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QuaternionFromHecke.lean#L64-L71","doc":"The Hecke eigenvalue pair (+q, -q⁻¹) on V ⊗ V, parameterised\nby the substrate parameter q. At q = 1, recovers the swap\neigenvalues (+1, -1). ","signatureChunk":0}]}